The connect-failure warning duplicates what the caller already knows. One line above it the
plugin emits connectError() with the very same status code over a BlockingQueuedConnection, so
every consumer has already been told, in full, before this reaches the log; ouaexp turns that
signal into its own translated message. Anyone reading the log therefore sees the same failure
twice, once in their language and once in English.

The message is also the only one in the plugin that prefixes itself with the product name --
which the qt.opcua.plugins.open62541 category already carries, reading "open62541: Open62541:
Failed to connect" -- and the only failure message that drops its status code, where its ~10
siblings end in UA_StatusCode_name().

Keep it as plugin diagnostics rather than a second warning: name the status like the rest of the
plugin does, and log it at debug level, where a consumer that ignores connectError() can still
reach it with qt.opcua.plugins.open62541.debug=true.

diff --git a/src/plugins/opcua/open62541/qopen62541backend.cpp b/src/plugins/opcua/open62541/qopen62541backend.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/opcua/open62541/qopen62541backend.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/opcua/open62541/qopen62541backend.cpp
@@ -1398,7 +1398,8 @@ void Open62541AsyncBackend::connectToEndpoint(const QOpcUaEndpointDescription &e
         emit QOpcUaBackend::connectError(&errorState);

         emit stateAndOrErrorChanged(QOpcUaClient::Disconnected, error);
-        qCWarning(QT_OPCUA_PLUGINS_OPEN62541) << "Open62541: Failed to connect";
+        // ouaexp patch: connectError() above already carried this status to the caller
+        qCDebug(QT_OPCUA_PLUGINS_OPEN62541) << "Failed to connect:" << UA_StatusCode_name(ret);
         return;
     }

